@c Current, curated application and integration guidance.
@node Emacs Packages
@chapter Applications And Integrations

@cindex applications
@cindex integrations
@cindex packages, speech support

Emacsvox prepares speech support for many Emacs modes as their libraries are
loaded.  Start the application normally; when its buffer appears, use
@kbd{C-h m} for the active modes and their commands, @kbd{C-h b} for the
effective bindings, and @kbd{C-h k} followed by a key to identify one binding.
The generated
@ref{Emacsvox Commands And Options,,,emacsvox-reference,Emacsvox Reference
Manual} records the public Emacsvox commands and options.

This chapter is a curated starting point, not a promise that every module in
the generated reference has a maintained task guide.  Emacs itself or a
third-party package owns the application's general operation; Emacsvox owns
the additional speech feedback.  Consult both sets of help when diagnosing a
problem.

Earlier Emacspeak surveys, including their W3, Dismal, and scanner/OCR setup,
are preserved as historical material in
@ref{Emacs Packages,Historical Application Survey,,emacsvox-heritage,Emacspeak
Heritage}.  They are not current setup instructions.

